You are working on the IEEE CMRU website (IEEE-CMRU-Website repo, ieee-cmru-website project), a Next.js App Router + TypeScript project.

STACK (do not deviate without asking):
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript
- Prisma ORM (never write raw SQL)
- NextAuth.js for admin auth (never hand-roll auth/session/password hashing)
- Zod for validation, always on both client AND server
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Deployed on Vercel

RULES:
- Never commit secrets. .env must stay in .gitignore. Always use process.env references.
- All /admin/* routes must be protected server-side (middleware or session check in the route/page itself), never just hidden in the UI.
- All API routes that accept user input must validate with Zod server-side, even if client-side validation exists.
- Do not introduce a second backend or hosting target. Everything lives in this one Next.js project on Vercel.
- Keep changes scoped to the specific file(s) or feature I ask about. Do not refactor unrelated files unless asked.
- When editing, prefer minimal, targeted diffs over rewriting whole files.
- There is a separate "frontend" repo (the old static HTML proposal version) that is archived and read-only — never modify it, only reference content/images copied from it when I paste them in.
